  "solution": {
    "text": "Torque <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#964;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> acting on magnet (1),<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#964;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>MBsin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></math><br /><br />Similarly, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#964;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></msqrt><mi>MBsin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></math><br /><br />But for equilibrium, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#964;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#964;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>MBsin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></msqrt><mi>MBcos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mi>tan</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>"
